Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:59:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Render the word popup senses through setText, not dynamic
 rows

The reconnaissance log ended the guesswork: the first sense row
measured 0x67 - zero width, correct height. The text was there all
along, laid out into an invisible sliver, in both the dark player
popup and the light reader popup (which also rules out any color
theory, as the user correctly reasoned). Neither removing the nested
ScrollView nor sizing the rows by content changed that: dynamically
added views simply do not measure properly inside this dialog.

The telling contrast sat in the same fill call all along: the
headline, the phonetic and the exam labels - XML views filled with
setText - rendered fine every round, at the exact moment the rows
next to them collapsed to zero width. The popup now uses only that
proven mechanism: the layout declares two content TextViews (senses
plus a secondary line for word forms and web translations) and fill
builds plain strings and calls setText, exactly like the exam labels.
The dynamic row machinery is gone.

Senses are capped at four lines and web translations at three, so a
word with many senses stays a quick-lookup popup; for words without
a dictionary entry the web translations take the primary spot. The
reconnaissance log now reports the senses view's measured size, and
the fill log reports the text lengths it set.
